Z||000000||Richard Parnell||05-07-2000||03:52 PM||||I put the new slave and master cyl on but can get no pressure in system. If I take the slave off the braket but still with hose hooked up and bleeder closed and then pump the clutch I immediately get pressure.  I then tried putting the slave back in place with the cylinder pushed in as it would sit normally, no pressure.  Bad slave?  The slave I put on is thicker and shorter than the one being replaced.  I'm about at my wits end on this one.||||reg||9
Z||000001||Phil||05-07-2000||07:42 PM||||If you took the slave off and the push rod extended all the way you shouldn't be able to push the pedal at all, the system will be in hydraulic lock-no movement anywhere. If you get pedal movement you've either got a leak or air in the lines.||||reg||1
